# Lasagna

Based on [https://www.delish.com/cooking/…](https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/recipes/a51337/classic-lasagna-recipe) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20241004050746/https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/recipes/a51337/classic-lasagna-recipe/))

{ rating="3" image="lasagna.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] [Standalone]{ ing="standalone" }

      - [ ] 12 oz [lasagna noodles]{ ing="lasagna-noodles" }
      - [ ] 1.5 lb [sliced or shredded mozzarella]{ ing="sliced-or-shredded-mozzarella" }
      - [ ] (Optional) 1-2 cup [spinach]{ ing="spinach" }
- [ ] [Meat/Sauce]{ ing="meat-sauce" }

      - [ ] (Optional) 1 lb [ground beef]{ ing="ground-beef" } (and/or spicy sausage)
      - [ ] 2 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
      - [ ] 1 tsp [dried oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }
      - [ ] 2 tsp [basil]{ ing="basil" }
      - [ ] [Kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }
      - [ ] Freshly [ground black pepper]{ ing="ground-black-pepper" }
      - [ ] 1-2 (32 oz) jars of [marinara]{ ing="marinara" }
- [ ] [Ricotta Cheese Mix]{ ing="ricotta-cheese-mix" }

      - [ ] 16 oz [whole milk ricotta]{ ing="whole-milk-ricotta" } (or cottage cheese)
      - [ ] 1/4 cup freshly [grated Parmesan]{ ing="grated-parmesan" }
      - [ ] 1/4 cup [chopped parsley]{ ing="chopped-parsley" }
- [ ] [Garnish]{ ing="garnish" }

      - [ ] 1/4 cup freshly [grated Parmesan]{ ing="grated-parmesan" }
      - [ ] 1/4 cup [chopped parsley]{ ing="chopped-parsley" }

## Recipe

1. On med-high heat, cook the meat ([ground beef]{ ing="ground-beef" } or [spinach]{ ing="spinach" }), breaking into small pieces with a wooden spoon until no longer pink
1. If the [noodles]{ ing="lasagna-noodles" } need to be boiled, prep boiling water and cook for only ~2 minutes until very al dente. May need to coat with a small amount of olive oil to prevent sticking
1. Pre-heat oven to 375
1. Drain and paper towel off any excess fat. In the same pan, add [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, spices ([oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }, [basil]{ ing="basil" }, [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }, and [pepper]{ ing="ground-black-pepper" }), and 1 jar of [marinara]{ ing="marinara" } sauce (save the rest)
1. In a mixing bowl, combine the [ricotta]{ ing="whole-milk-ricotta" }, [Parmesan]{ ing="grated-parmesan" }, and [parsley]{ ing="chopped-parsley" }. Season with [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" } and [pepper]{ ing="ground-black-pepper" }
1. In a large casserole dish, spread thin layers of meat sauce/[noodles]{ ing="lasagna-noodles" }/[ricotta]{ ing="whole-milk-ricotta" } [mix]{ ing="ricotta-cheese-mix" }/sliced [mozzarella]{ ing="sliced-or-shredded-mozzarella" }. Repeat about 4 times until all of the noodles are used (ricotta should finish on n-1 layers). If needed, add additional [marinara]{ ing="marinara" } sauce
1. Top last layer of [noodles]{ ing="lasagna-noodles" } with meat sauce, then [Parmesan]{ ing="grated-parmesan" } and [mozzarella]{ ing="sliced-or-shredded-mozzarella" }
1. Cover with foil and bake for 15 minutes. Increase to 400 and bake uncovered for 20 min - *see notes for aluminum pans
1. [Garnish]{ ing="garnish" } with [parsley]{ ing="chopped-parsley" } and [basil]{ ing="basil" }

## Notes

1. In a dark aluminum pan, i needed to extend the cook time from 15 covered/20 uncovered min to 25/35 min to soften the noodles, which came pre-cooked
